N={141:'The paired bodily reaction marks being left unable to answer or act; the cases apply it to patriarchs, buddhas, and exposed participants rather than diagnosing literal illness.',142:'The proverb attributes unease or self-exposure to the guilty thief; later speakers quote it as an appraisal, not as evidence of an actual theft.',143:'The answer places the great road through the capital itself; the cases retain this ordinary route image while asking where the Way is.',144:'The violent formula threatens complete division of a person, view, or answer; it is rhetoric in the retained sermons and appraisals, not a narrated execution.',145:'The sailing image means adjusting action to the wind or conditions; cases can praise responsive skill or criticize merely opportunistic adaptation.',146:'The paired reduplications describe being completely bare and uncovered; the records apply them to a condition with nothing available to grasp.',147:'The verdict groups people or positions for a single burial; its targets vary, so the phrase does not by itself say why they deserve the same disposal.',148:'The image joins forceful probing of bones with extracting marrow; records use it for exacting instruction, investigation, and adept handling rather than literal anatomy.',149:'The couplet makes lesser heights and streams reach their limit at the great mountain and sea; it is retained as a paired convergence image.',150:'The idiom describes elusive, extraordinary appearing and disappearing; speakers use it for mobile action, verbal action, and appraisals without asserting supernatural beings literally act.'}
Z={141:'Yuanwu and Yinyuan say even Linji, Deshan, buddhas, or patriarchs are left staring and agape; other records turn the same reaction on a participant whose move is exposed.',142:'Baofu’s appraisal of Cuiyan’s summer-end question becomes a repeatedly raised proverb, while Zhimen uses it after asking whether anyone watched the abbot’s room.',143:'Zhaozhou answers his questioner, who rejects the road outside and asks for the great road; later sermons quote, verse, and redeploy his Chang’an answer.',144:'Speakers cut views, challengers, or even a hypothetical Daruma into three, making the formula a severe verdict on what has just been proposed.',145:'Yuanwu praises the World-Honored One for setting sail with the wind, while Xuedou and other appraisers can use the same sailing skill as a lower, condition-following move.',146:'Hall discourses place the paired bareness beside having nothing to grasp, before birth and after birth, or as a view that itself still requires examination.',147:'Masters use one-pit burial to reject paired figures, rival moves, or an answer and its alternatives together, announcing common disposal rather than separate adjudication.',148:'Huike recalls ancient seekers striking bones for marrow; later masters apply the same image to penetrating instruction, lineage style, and forceful scrutiny.',149:'Masters use the mountain-and-sea couplet after demands for a beyond-rank statement, in answers across traditions, and as a questioner’s advance that is sometimes dismissed as idle talk.',150:'The records apply the idiom to Guanyin’s activity, Zhaozhou’s answer, mobile teaching action, and the transformations attributed to a capable person.'}
BODY={141:'The witnesses attach the same staring eyes and open mouth to being stopped, exposed, or unable to respond across sermons, verse, and appraisal.',142:'The retained cases include Baofu’s original appraisal, later quotations of it, and direct uses after suspicious or self-revealing conduct.',143:'Zhaozhou’s question-and-answer frame anchors the phrase; later records preserve it as quotation, verse line, and direct redeployment.',144:'Across the cases, the object threatened with threefold division changes, but the complete cutting verdict and its severity remain stable.',145:'The cases preserve both poles of the sailing idiom: skill in responding to conditions and criticism of action governed only by those conditions.',146:'All witnesses retain the two coordinated bareness terms, often beside nothing to grasp or no covering left, rather than treating either reduplication alone as the formula.',147:'The reviewed cases direct the one-pit burial at different pairs or positions, confirming a shared-disposal verdict without fixing one fixed target.',148:'Biographical recollection, hall speech, and lineage appraisal all preserve the bone-to-marrow sequence as a figure for penetrating or exacting action.',149:'Both clauses recur together: peaks terminate at the great mountain and streams lose their sound at the sea, giving parallel land and water convergence.',150:'The cases distribute the idiom across direct speech, commentary, verse, and portrait praise while preserving its sense of elusive, unconstrained activity.'}
